; =============================================================================
; TONE DATABASE - TONE/VOICE PARAMETER RECORDS (ToneRec_000 .. ToneRec_628)
; =============================================================================
; 579 variable-length tone records tiling ROM 0x8324D4-0x855A47 with no gaps
; or padding.  They are the payload behind the 629-entry stream-offset table
; at 0x831B00: each table entry is a LE32 offset relative to the database base
; 0x830000.  At boot, SubCPU_Send_Payload (maincpu) copies 0x830000-0x87FFFF
; into SubCPU RAM at 0x50000, so the SubCPU sees these records at 0x524D4+.
;
; Pointer resolution (subcpu DSP1_ResolveStreamPtr):
;   ptr = 0x50000 + LE32[0x51B00 + 4*(arg + bias)],  bias = word @0x50088 = 0x152
; so table index = caller's stream number + 338.  Index map:
;   000-309  reached with negative stream numbers (-338..-29)
;   310-337  drum kits (0x863079+) and drawbar records (0x8706BD+); those
;            targets are OUTSIDE this module (see the aux-tables region)
;   338-377  stream numbers 0-39 (the 5-block flagship tones)
;   378-399  stream numbers 40-61: duplicate offsets of index 0 ("Piano"),
;            i.e. unused live-slot entries falling back to the default tone
;   400-628  stream numbers 62-290 (GM-style bank, ends with "Gun Shot")
;
; Records are labeled ToneRec_NNN, NNN = zero-padded decimal table index (the
; same scheme the 0x831B00 table module uses).  This file is in ADDRESS order,
; which is index order 000-309, then 400-628, then 338-377.
;
; RECORD LAYOUT (record length = 21 + 81*N bytes, N = 1..5 blocks; the length
; is implied by the distance to the next record's table offset - no explicit
; size field was found):
;   +0x00  16-byte space-padded ASCII tone name
;   +0x10  5-byte layer-configuration field: bytes 0-3 hold 2-bit sub-fields
;          whose values are only ever 0 or 1 (semantics undetermined; the
;          popcount matches the block count for 311 of 579 records, so it is
;          NOT a plain block count); byte 4 is 0x55 in all 579 records
;   +0x15  81-byte COMMON block: starts 0x81 0x40 in all 579 records; block
;          offsets +8,+9,+11,+12,+36,+48,+52,+53,+64,+68,+69 are always 0x00
;          and +10,+13 always 0x40
;   +0x66  zero to four further 81-byte LAYER blocks (per-layer parameters)
;
; FIELD OBSERVATIONS (from sibling records differing in one known property):
;   layer block +19: semitone offset - "Piano"=66, "Piano 1 Octave"=54,
;       "Piano 2 Octave"=42 (12 per octave; block offsets +48/+73 track it)
;   layer block +54/+55/+62/+69: differ between "Piano" and "Bright Piano",
;       so timbre/filter-related
;   subcpu DSP_Reinit_VoiceSlots always copies 0xD5 words (426 bytes, the
;       maximum record size) from the resolved pointer, over-reading into the
;       following record for shorter tones
;
; RECORD LAYOUT FROM THE READERS (2026-09-25).  Where this disagrees with the
; text above, this is the reading of the code; the older lines are kept and each
; disagreement is marked CORRECTED.  Subcpu addresses are v1.42.
;
; HOW A RECORD IS REACHED.  ToneDB_Find_PatchRecord (0x031F71) resolves a
; (bank selector, program) pair through ToneDB_BankMap_Main and the tone-number
; banks (tone_database_directory.s) to a table index and returns ToneDB_Base +
; ToneDB_ToneOffsetTable[index]; ToneDB_Find_ToneRecord_CoeffPath (0x031F16)
; does the same through the Coeff banks.  VoiceParam_Update_InactivePath
; (0x0321E5) stores the pointer in the part record at +0x06 (0x04136E +
; part*0x11F).  Each record's two-line header names the bank/program(s) that
; select it.
;
;   +0x00  16-char name
;   +0x10  PART-MODE BYTE.  Voice_SetVelocity (0x02C8E4) switches on +0x10 &
;          0xC0: 0x00 = the four-partial melodic path, which is every record in
;          this file; 0x40 = the drawbar records, 0x80 = the drum kits (both in
;          tone_database_aux.s), 0xC0 = silent.  Bit 4 is tested by
;          Voice_Calc_LevelPair_PatchAtk (0x025636) through voice slot +0x13
;          (set -> bit 15 of slot +0x01 cleared, clear -> set).  Census: 0x00
;          x68, 0x10 x134, 0x20 x217, 0x30 x160.
;   +0x11  PARTIAL MASK.  Partial p (0..3) is present iff +0x11 & {0x01, 0x04,
;          0x10, 0x40}[p] (the table at subcpu 0x00FB4E).  For a ROM bank
;          selector VoiceBuf_TypeSelector_MatchEpilogue (0x032082) returns the
;          partial's RANK = the number of present partials among 1..p, and
;          EFFSlotScan_AssignPath (0x032295) binds it to rec + 0x66 +
;          0x51*rank in the part record at +0x6E + 0x25*p; an absent partial is
;          bound to ToneDB_DefaultLayerParams (dir +0xAC) instead.
;          CORRECTED: the "+0x10 5-byte layer-configuration field" above is
;          three fields, and its "popcount matches the block count for 311 of
;          579" counted bytes that are not the mask.  popcount(+0x11 & 0x55) is
;          exactly N-1 in 542 of the 579 records: all 519 with N <= 4 and the
;          23 N=5 records outside the staging streams.  The other 37 are
;          staging-stream records, see STAGING STREAMS below.
;   +0x12  read by Partial_Build_Present_Word (0x032B1E), which tests bits 1:0
;          (0 in every record; the byte is 0x00 x565, 0x40 x13, 0x10 x1);
;          Voice_PitchBend_BranchB (0x02A64C) takes its address.
;   +0x13  bend type (0 x573, 4 x6), read by Voice_Pitch_Compute_Inactive
;          (0x023698); +0x14 (0x55 in all 579): Voice_PitchBend_BranchA
;          (0x02A62E) takes its address, no value read found.
;   +0x15  81-byte COMMON block.  Readers found (record offsets; through the
;          part's tone pointer at part +0x06 or voice slot +0x13):
;            +0x27+2c  {wave, slot} byte pairs (ToneDB_Find_SubToneRecord
;                      0x032AE0 -- a drum kit's per-note map; a melodic record
;                      reaches it only for keys >= 0x78 on a SET whose flags
;                      bit 1 is set, see ToneDB_EnvDescTable)
;            +0x29     low nibble = octave-shift index (Voice_Pitch_Compute
;                      0x023584 -> Pitch_Get_Patch_Octave_Shift; 8 x494)
;            +0x2A     high and low nibble each index the byte table 0x011ACF
;                      (Instrument_LookupProgram_HiNibble 0x02289D / _LoNibble
;                      0x0228D9)
;            +0x2B+4k  (k = 0..3) byte +2 bit 7 tested by
;                      ExtVoice_Build_SlotRegisters (0x024BE3)
;            +0x5C     level offset centred on 0x40 (Level_Build_Reg0C0 0x0253FE)
;            +0x5D     algorithm type, low nibble (AlgoType_StateWrite 0x033557,
;                      Partial_Build_Present_Word)
;            +0x5E..+0x61  Voice_Build_Partial_Descriptor (0x02B717, ROM tables
;                      0x012038/0x012057/0x012095); +0x5E/+0x60 also
;                      DSP_ChanFreq_WritePacket1 (0x033B8B, algorithm types 6/7),
;                      +0x5F & 0x3F AlgoType_AB_LoadIndex (0x033B70, types 0x0A/0x0B)
;            +0x64, +0x65  Voice_SecondaryParam_Path2 (0x033DAA) / _Epilogue
;                      (0x033DD3)
;          The rest of the common block has no reader found.
;   +0x66  N-1 81-byte PARTIAL BLOCKS in rank order.  A bound block becomes the
;          voice slot's paramA (slot +0x17, stored by
;          Voice_Build_Partial_Descriptor) and is read, in the field groups the
;          rows below are cut into, by the melodic voice path
;          (Voice_Build_Register_Set 0x02B4E3, Voice_Release_Type4 0x02BCD6):
;     blk+0x00..+0x06  +0x02/+0x03 wave-select pair (WaveSel_StageA1_FromPatchBlock
;                      0x0325FC); DSP_WriteAlgoBuffer (0x03522E) forces +0x03
;                      bits 5:4 to 1 unless bits 7:6 = 11 when it stages a part;
;                      +0x00 is read by Voice_Build_GateCommand (0x025589) and
;                      Voice_ComputePitch, +0x05 by Pitch_Apply_Partial_Detune
;                      (0x023A05)
;     blk+0x07..+0x16  ENVELOPE 2: Voice_Level_ComputeTriplet (0x023AD0, TG
;                      r0x24..0x26) reads +0x07 (a sign flag), +0x09/+0x0B/+0x0D
;                      segment targets with +0x0A/+0x0C/+0x0E, +0x11 key scale,
;                      +0x13 velocity baseline, +0x14/+0x15 velocity depths;
;                      Voice_Calc_LevelPair_EGB (0x026975) +0x0F/+0x10/+0x16;
;                      Voice_PortaLevel_Compute (0x0248D5) +0x08
;     blk+0x17..+0x26  PITCH: +0x17 channel detune (Voice_ApplyPortamento
;                      0x026637); +0x18 signed detune, +0x19 curve selector
;                      (0xE0 = the direct note table), +0x1A..+0x1C
;                      (Voice_ComputePitch 0x026396); +0x1D..+0x26 no reader found
;     blk+0x27..+0x35  ENVELOPE 1, amplitude: Voice_Calc_LevelPair_PatchAtk
;                      (0x025636), _Full (0x025C87), _Mono (0x025F7F) read three
;                      (target, rate) segments +0x27..+0x2C, key scale +0x2E/
;                      +0x2F, the velocity control triple +0x30..+0x32 and
;                      depths +0x33/+0x34; Voice_Calc_LevelPair_EGA (0x026769)
;                      +0x2D level and +0x35
;     blk+0x36..+0x3C  FILTER CONTROL: +0x36 bits 2:0 = the filter builder
;                      TVF_Build_Dispatch (0x024102) runs, bits 7:5 = key-follow
;                      curve; +0x37 key-follow depth; +0x39..+0x3B level-scaling
;                      offset/low/high and +0x3C its depth (TVF_Calc_Cutoff 0x022C06)
;     blk+0x3D..+0x4C  ENVELOPE 3: Voice_StereoLevel_Compute (0x024664) reads
;                      +0x3D shared bias, +0x3F..+0x44 three (target, rate)
;                      segments, +0x47 key scale, +0x49 velocity baseline,
;                      +0x4A/+0x4B depths; Voice_Calc_LevelPair_EGC (0x026AAA)
;                      +0x45/+0x46/+0x4C; Voice_PortaLevel_Compute +0x3E
;     blk+0x4D..+0x50  FILTER REGISTERS: +0x4D cutoff seed, +0x4E slope/mode,
;                      +0x4F/+0x50 resonance/depth pair, or a second cutoff in
;                      mode 5 (TVF_Build_Full 0x023D01, Voice_PitchPack_Mode2
;                      0x023DB5 .. _Mode5_Dual 0x02403D)
;          Envelopes 2 and 3 are one 16-byte structure placed 0x36 apart
;          (+0x07 <-> +0x3D, +0x09 <-> +0x3F, +0x11 <-> +0x47, +0x13 <-> +0x49).
;          No reader found for blk +0x01, +0x04, +0x06, +0x12, +0x1D..+0x26,
;          +0x38, +0x48.  Per-offset readers, split by voice path:
;          python3 notes/tonedb-2026-09-25/partial_block_reads.py --chains
;          CORRECTED: "layer block +19: semitone offset" above.  blk +0x13 is
;          envelope 2's velocity baseline and +0x30 / +0x49 hold the same role
;          for envelopes 1 and 3; that the three move together with the octave
;          variants (66/54/42) is a fact about the data, but the code does not
;          use them as a pitch offset.
;
; STAGING STREAMS.  The 40 records at table indices 338-377 are the ones the
; full rebuild in DSP_Reinit_VoiceSlots (A = 0xFF: streams 0..0x27 through
; DSP1_ResolveStreamPtr 0x0351E2) copies, 0xD5 words = 426 bytes each, into the
; RAM image at (0x04531C) = 0x007800 + 0x10 + 0x1D6*stream
; (DSP_ResetWriteBufferPtr 0x03555F sets that pointer).  The 0x72AA-byte image
; is exchanged with the maincpu's battery-backed SRAM at 0x1E0000 by E1
; transfers on both sides.  All 40 are stored at the full 426 bytes whatever
; their mask -- 37 carry blocks that no partial of the ROM mask is bound to --
; so, CORRECTING the line above, that copy never over-reads into the next
; record.  Which streams the single-stream path (A*0x14 + C) can reach is not
; established here.
; =============================================================================

